Aerodome is a prediction-based air defense algorithm which uses machine learning to predict the likelihood 
of future threats with passive input. 
Objectives: 
1. To read and analyze raw historical air intrusion data on an excel sheet 
2. To train and develop a machine learning model using libraries in Python 
3. To use the model in predicting threats and conducting threat assessment using incoming data 
4. To visualize the processed data in graphs and charts 
5. Implement mathematical prediction algorithms on the data 
6. To store the results in a cloud storage platform 
Unlike traditional air defense systems that respond to existing threats, Mjolnir uses machine learning and 
mathematical prediction models to forecast the probability of penetration, allowing for suitabke defensive 
measures to be taken. 
Libraries Used: 
● NumPy: For complex mathematical and statistical operations 
● Openpyxl: To open and read .xlsx files 
● Pandas: For reading and manipulating excel data 
● SciKit-learn: Machine learning library to train and develop the model 
● Joblib: To save and load machine learning models 
● io: For processing live data 
● Google Cloud Storage: To save results in google cloud 
● AsaPy: For aerospace simulation integration (potentially used)
